+Rainfall and Flooding
+       In Florida, Debby produced a large swath of 5–10 inches of rainfall that extended from
+west-central Florida northward to the Florida Big Bend (Fig. 10). Locally higher amounts of 10–15
+inches occurred near and to the south of the Tampa Bay region, with the highest total in the state
+(16.98 inches) reported in Sarasota. Isolated totals greater than 12 inches were reported in
+northern Florida near and to the east of the track of the center. Debby also produced a large swath
